*Mitigation of SSRF

Blacklist are a poor methodolody of handleling SSRF. The best methods to handle this form of vurnerability is to Whitelist the hostnames (DNS name) or IP address that is required of your application. If a blacklist is necessary you must properly validate user input.

Eliminated or disable any unesed schemas. if your application on relys on HTTP or HTTPS only allow those schemas. The threat actor will be unable to use the web application to make dangerous request such as  file:///, dict://, ftp://, and gopher://

